{
  "content": "<p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Dennis Freeman</p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong> The concept of the Fourier series can be applied to aperiodic functions by treating it as a periodic function with period T = infinity. This new transform has some key similarities and differences with the Laplace transform, its properties, and domains.</p>\n",
